data.content:
Here are the three EF Core 10 breaking changes affecting your code and their fixes:

---

## 1. `ExecuteUpdateAsync` — now accepts a regular lambda (not an expression tree)

Your expression tree construction code won't compile. Replace it with a simple lambda:

```csharp
// .NET 10 — no more expression tree plumbing
await context.Blogs.ExecuteUpdateAsync(s =>
{
    s.SetProperty(b => b.Views, 8);
    if (nameChanged)
    {
        s.SetProperty(b => b.Name, "foo");
    }
});
```

---

## 2. Complex type column names are now uniquified/use full path

Two changes hit you:
- **Duplicate property names** (e.g., `ShippingAddress.Street` and `BillingAddress.Street`) now get a numeric suffix.
- **Nested complex types** use the full path: `Order.Payment.BillingAddress.City` maps to `Payment_BillingAddress_City` (was `BillingAddress_City`).

A migration will be generated to rename columns. To **keep existing column names**, pin them explicitly:

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Customer>(b =>
{
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.ShippingAddress, sa =>
        sa.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("ShippingAddress_Street"));
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.BillingAddress, ba =>
        ba.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("BillingAddress_Street"));
});

// Nested example — preserve old name
modelBuilder.Entity<Order>(b =>
{
    b.ComplexProperty(o => o.Payment, p =>
        p.ComplexProperty(pay => pay.BillingAddress, ba =>
            ba.Property(a => a.City).HasColumnName("BillingAddress_City")));
});
```

---

## 3. `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` — new `logCommandText` parameter

Every method gained a `string logCommandText` parameter at the end:

```csharp
public class MyLogger : IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger
{
    public InterceptionResult<DbDataReader> CommandReaderExecuting(
        IRelationalConnection connection,
        DbCommand command,
        DbContext context,
        Guid commandId,
        Guid connectionId,
        DateTimeOffset startTime,
        string logCommandText)   // ← add this
    {
        // logCommandText contains redacted SQL safe for logging
        // command.CommandText has the actual SQL
    }
}
```

Update all method signatures in your implementation (`CommandReaderExecuted`, `CommandScalarExecuting`, etc.) similarly.
